{"type":"text","timestamp":1790375319339,"sessionID":"ses_f2553ebd8ffepFy5PYvXjauNAn","part":{"id":"prt_0daaf5711001LNh6mjHJl9rXyw","messageID":"msg_0daaf24f4001T4g9eUP572uT5E","sessionID":"ses_f2553ebd8ffepFy5PYvXjauNAn","type":"text","text":"Implemented the combat-targeting setup.\n\n- Added the opposing-team group mapping in [unit_stats.gd](/workspace/data/units/unit_stats.gd).\n- Created [DetectRange](/workspace/custom_nodes/detect_range.gd) with the requested collision layers, masks, and circular range scaling. The default base range is 32 pixels.\n- Created [TargetFinder](/workspace/custom_nodes/target_finder.gd) with range tracking, change signals, nearest-opponent selection using squared distance, and `has_target_in_range()`.\n- Wired both nodes into [battle_unit.tscn](/workspace/scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.tscn) and exposed them through [battle_unit.gd](/workspace/scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd), including stats propagation.\n\nVerified with Godot 4.4.1: project import and startup passed, and [runtime checks](/workspace/scripts/verify_targeting.gd) passed for both teams, entry/exit signals, stats updates, non-unit filtering, and empty target groups. The [debug capture](/workspace/targeting_verification.png) confirms the near enemy is within the player’s detection range and the far enemy is outside it.","time":{"start":1790375319313,"end":1790375319316},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0536e0f7a7541c92016ab6f58f0b14819095f5be651bc6e448","phase":"final_answer"}}}}
